	"title"		"Bugfix: Establish a Trade – Location Rank Fix (1.2.5)"
	"description"		"[h1]Bugfix: Establish a Trade – Location Rank Fix[/h1]

Fixes the [b]Develop a Capital Economy[/b] mission task [b]Establish a Trade[/b] so that [b]Town and City locations are correctly selectable[/b] as the mission description intends.

[h2]The Bug[/h2]
In vanilla 1.2.5, the task's location filter uses [code]rank_index <= 1[/code], which only matches Megalopolis and City locations and wrongly rejects Towns. The rank_index values (confirmed from the game files) are:
[list]
[*] 0 = Megalopolis (highest)
[*] 1 = City
[*] 2 = Town
[*] 3 = Rural Settlement (lowest)
[/list]
The game's own definition of an urban location is [code]rank_index < 3[/code] (Megalopolis, City, or Town). The vanilla [code]<= 1[/code] excludes Town-rank locations, so a Town shows an [b]X[/b] and the task cannot be completed there.

[h2]The Fix[/h2]
Changes [code]rank_index <= 1[/code] to [code]rank_index <= 2[/code] in two places in the mission file: the [i]select_trigger visible[/i] block (which locations appear selectable) and the [i]enabled[/i] block of the downstream [i]mission_prepare_industry_focus[/i] task (which gates the next step). This matches the game's own [code]location_is_urban[/code] filter — Megalopolis, City and Town are selectable; Rural Settlements remain excluded.

[h2]Source[/h2]
[list]
[*] Developer-confirmed report: https://forum.paradoxplaza.com/forum/threads/develop-a-capital-economy-mission-task-establish-a-trade-requires-a-rural-location-instead-of-town-or-city.1920958/
[*] Rank-index thread: https://forum.paradoxplaza.com/forum/threads/location-rank-index-less-than-1.1920949/
[/list]
Only the single condition is changed. All other mission content is unmodified vanilla.

[b]Note:[/b] Enabling any mod changes the game checksum, which disables achievements and blocks multiplayer with unmodded clients."
	"changenote"		"Bump to v1.2: correct short_description (was incorrectly describing the fix as >= 1; actual fix is <= 2). No functional change to the mission file."
}
